---
title: "run.py: base check and assumption sensitivity pass"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  s0: The command runs the base TLC check
  s1: The command rechecks holding rules without the first assumption
  s2: The command writes the report and exits
  s3: The command rechecks holding rules without the second assumption
  s4: The command rechecks surviving rules without either assumption
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: every rule holds in the base check (exit 0) or some rules hold and others break (exit 1)
  s0 --> s2: every rule breaks in the base check (exit 1) or the base check fails (exit 2)
  s1 --> s3: the first assumption check finishes
  s3 --> s2: every base-holding rule already broke under one relaxation
  s3 --> s4: some base-holding rules survived both single checks
  s4 --> s2: the combined assumption check finishes
